{
    "background_story": "Asher was a majestic Friesian stallion with a gleaming black coat and a flowing mane. He was bred for the elegant art of haute \u00e9cole, where precision and control were paramount. Asher's rider, a skilled dressage competitor, spent years training him to perfect the encolure, a delicate maneuver where the horse bends his neck and body in a fluid, circular motion. With each passing competition, Asher's mastery of the encolure grew, earning him and his rider numerous accolades. But Asher's true beauty lay not just in his athleticism, but in the bond he shared with his rider, a partnership built on trust, respect, and a deep understanding of each other's movements. Together, they danced across the arena, their encolure a testament to the harmony between horse and rider.",
